Supported vector index methods include HNSW, IVF and DiskANN. Example index creation (MongoDB 7.0-style vector index):

db.products.createIndex(
  { embedding: "vector" },
  {
    name: "embedding_vector_idx",
    vector: {
      dimensions: 1536,
      similarity: "cosine",
      method: "hnsw",
      methodOptions: { m: 16, efConstruction: 200 }
    }
  }
)

(Adjust dimensions and methodOptions to your embedding size and performance needs.)

Create a vector index on the embedding field. Example (MongoDB 7.0-style):

db.products.createIndex(
  { embedding: "vector" },
  {
    name: "embedding_vector_idx",
    vector: {
      dimensions: 1536,
      similarity: "cosine",
      method: "hnsw",
      methodOptions: { m: 16, efConstruction: 200 }
    }
  }
)

(Adjust dimensions to your embedding size.)

Use a vector KNN aggregation stage (if supported) such as knnBeta/$vectorSearch. Example aggregation (conceptual):

db.products.aggregate([
  { $vectorSearch: { k: 5, vector: <queryVector>, path: "embedding", similarity: "cosine" } },
  { $project: { score: { $meta: "searchScore" }, name: 1, sku: 1, embedding: 0 } }
])

If a $vectorSearch/$knn stage is not available, fall back to client-side cosine calculation on a candidate set returned by a lightweight filter or random sampling.
